# PR110: independent modern invariant mechanism priority audit

The modern bodies actually read do not supply an earlier full covering theorem for the literal k603 assertion. They provide important ingredients and closely related invariants. They do not make the target ordinary antipedal radial sum a stated corollary without an additional observable-specific identification.

There is one essential selected-candidate version gap: the complete journal final of Garcia–Koiller–Reznik, *Estimating Elliptic Billiard Invariants with Spatial Integrals*, DOI [10.1007/s10883-022-09608-y](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10883-022-09608-y), remains unread. Its complete 2021 precursor was read, but a changed title/abstract and a publisher first-page preview do not authenticate the final body. Consequently this report gives bounded support within its read corpus, not combined priority or publication clearance. It supplies no evidence warranting an `already_solved` classification.

## Pinned object and independence

PR110, problem5100032 / AMR-050-0032, original head3d159f0a00d0bd7ff8d558d6fbc75af5094f7a35. Original PROOF body SHA256:8478d2a792944c5fb9e8a53324e0c6bce8eba317de29c31a6fcbd6ca0205709d. The source/mathematical gate is an input, not a priority conclusion. The original 2/5 effort and zero new central proof-search turns are retained.

For an outer ellipse a>b>0 and fixed strictly nested confocal elliptical caustic0<lambda<b², take every regular closed billiard/Poncelet orbit, including admissible stars, reversals, and repeated traversals. At each focus, intersect the consecutive supporting lines through vertices perpendicular to their focus rays. The target says the two sums of ordinary positive Euclidean radial distances are finite and equal, so their ratio is1. It does not claim each separate sum is constant with phase. The verified norm difference per edge is a fixed coefficient times the ordinate increment.

This family independently tested modern complexification, support/generating functions, focal inversion, bicentric/pedal duality, projective monodromy, harmonic-polygon transforms, motion/grid invariants, integrability and recent isogonal constructions. No other fresh family report was read. Root's discovery aid for the 2026 isogonal paper was a source lead; its actual primary body was inspected independently. No Git mutation, status change, outreach, manuscript authoring, or publication occurred.

## The prior theorem comparison

